% references.bib
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% HOW TO USE THIS FILE
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% 1. In Zotero: select your sources → right-click → Export Items
%    → Format: BibTeX → save as references.bib → replace this file.
%
% 2. To cite in a .qmd file: [@AuthorYear]
%    Examples:
%      [@Entman1993]          → (Entman, 1993)
%      [@Entman1993, p. 52]   → (Entman, 1993, p. 52)
%      @Entman1993            → Entman (1993)  [narrative cite]
%
% 3. Only sources you actually cite will appear in the References
%    chapter. Unused entries are silently ignored.
%
% 4. The entries below are pre-loaded common methods and theory
%    sources. Add your own entries below them.
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

